#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD2212 expect=noViolation domain=TS
#note "EMPTY-DATASET PIN, re-noted under PLAN-zero-row-routing-rekey.md (owner rulings Q1 / Q5 / 6c-1, Fix #349 / EC-89; policy text: lib/corej-cdisc-rules/documentation/zero-row-policy.md). The conditional counter-face to PMDA-SD2207's 0-row fire: a DECLARED 0-row TS. Ruled (Q1): a rule that can decide CORRECTLY without reading a row fires on an empty dataset exactly as on a populated one -- this Check is two dataset facts ($STYPE_INTERVENTIONAL >= 1 and $tindtp_count == 0, both record_count operations), decided by BroadcastFold upstream of the row path and never by the retired synthetic table. Here the condition side is false ($STYPE_INTERVENTIONAL = 0, 0 >= 1 is false) -> SILENT by the rule's own logic, not by a zero-row short-circuit. The empty TS is reported once, by PMDA-SD0001. Escalate if it fires: that would mean record_count stopped counting an empty dataset as 0."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset TS label="Trial Summary"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col TSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TSPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter Short Name"
col TSPARM   type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter"
col TSVAL    type=Char label="Parameter Value"
---
